// THREAT-MODEL.md section 4.5, row B8 (verified by a build, not a `check`).
// `kryos build --cache` consults the artifact cache BEFORE the capability
// checker, and the cache key (source hash, target, mode, output type, compiler
// version) does not include the capability mode. So:
//   1. `kryos build x.kry`                                   -> rejected, E0505
//   2. `kryos build --capabilities-mode=permissive --cache x.kry` -> built, cached
//   3. `kryos build --cache x.kry` (default mode)            -> cache hit, built
//      (`--strict-capabilities --cache` also hits the same entry)
// Step 3 is the same source step 1 rejected. check-escapes-documented.sh runs
// these three steps with KRYOS_CACHE_DIR pointing at a scratch directory.
// (Executed 2026-11-01: rc 1, 0, 0.)
fn main() {
    println("home=" + env_get("PATH"))
}
